<title>USA: Oglebay Norton buys two vessels.</title>
<headline>Oglebay Norton buys two vessels.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oglebay Norton Co said Friday it has bought two vessels from GATX Capital Corp for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>The company said the two vessels -- the M/V David Z Norton and the M/V Wolverine -- are 630-foot-long self-unloading ships that carry iron ore, coal and stone on the Great Lakes.</p>
<p>The company had been leasing the two from GATX under agreements that were to expire in 1998 and 1999, it said.</p>
